WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.640
Don't think that
you'll be able to survive...

3
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.380
after making the entire
world your enemy!

4
00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.470
Bring it on!

5
00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.770
<b>Jump into the Waterfall!!</b>

6
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:13.730
<b>Plaza Outside the Courthouse</b>

7
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.740
<b>Left Tower
(Mozu and Lulu)</b>

8
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.650
Okay! We pulled the lever!

9
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.750
We did it-waina!

10
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.720
<b>Right Tower
(Kiwi and Tilestone)</b>

11
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.510
Looks like Mozu and the
others got it done, too-waina.

12
00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.260
Go, Straw Hat!

13
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.640
The drawbridge is coming down!

14
00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.000
Looks like they pulled through.

15
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.700
Good timing.

16
00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.970
I-I'm trembling with anticipation!

17
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.360
Lower that bridge already.

18
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.040
You look evil.

19
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.370
Robin!

20
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.330
We won't stop until we rescue you!

21
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.290
Stay over there!

22
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.630
They're in high spirits.

23
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.030
To think that they don't fear
the flag of the government...

24
00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:23.590
How pointless.

25
00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:26.760
There's no way
that they could defeat us.

26
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.120
Don't you cross!

27
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.330
The drawbridge is coming down!

28
00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.770
Go! Straw Hat!

29
00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.550
Curse those pirates!

30
00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.110
Like we'd let that happen!

31
00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.460
Get the mortar ready!

32
00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.450
Stop the drawbridge!
Break it if you have to!

33
00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.660
I'm not gonna let you do that!

34
00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.870
Pipe Hitch Knives!

35
00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.220
This is the end of you!

36
00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.360
Demolition Chop!

37
00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.070
Chief Justice Baskerville!

38
00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.110
Too bad!

39
00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.700
We're actually
the chief justice trio!

40
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.410
What?!

41
00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.870
I, the left Baskerville,
am named Bas!

42
00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.330
I, the right Baskerville,
am named Kerville!

43
00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.580
And I, the center Baskerville,
go by the name...

44
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.840
Princess!

45
00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.300
What're ya talkin' about?!

46
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.750
So they were just stuck together?

47
00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.260
What for?!

48
00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.220
We're good friends!

49
00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.830
Shut up!

50
00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.680
Fire the mortar!

51
00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.070
The drawbridge stopped?!

52
00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.760
Gettin' in our way!

53
00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.030
Those bastards!

54
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.590
Who did this?!

55
00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.860
Chief Spandam!

56
00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.310
Please evacuate
from the Tower of Justice!

57
00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.630
All right! Good job!

58
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.740
I'm gonna head to the Gates of Justice
before they come over to this side!

59
00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.510
Come, Nico Robin!

60
00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.770
Someone! Bring Cutty Flam!

61
00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.140
Robin!

62
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.900
Those pirates are nobodies.

63
00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:45.670
I've got the assassin group
CP9 on my side!

64
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.870
Nico Robin, a survivor
of the island of scholars...

65
00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.750
who schemed to bring back
the ancient weapons...

66
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:57.540
Cutty Flam, who inherited
an ancient weapon's blueprints...

67
00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.700
I'm definitely not gonna stand back and
miss this opportunity to gain more power!

68
00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.060
Cutty Flam...

69
00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.650
That's...

70
00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.350
Hey... don't tell me...

71
00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.940
Those are the ancient
weapon Pluton's blueprints...!

72
00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.080
They're the real deal.

73
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.570
Do you believe me?

74
00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:37.500
Lucci... Kaku...
You guys can tell, right?

75
00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.590
I thought it was unlikely...

76
00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:55.560
So you were hiding them
inside your body, huh?

77
00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.420
T-The real ones?!

78
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.980
Are those the real ones?!

79
00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.240
Hand them over...
Hand them over to me!

80
00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.180
Those are my long sought-after
blueprints!

81
00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.570
Nico Robin.

82
00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.930
Rumors are such unreliable things,
aren't they?

83
00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.480
While we were being
brought to this damn place,

84
00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.100
I came to realize
that you aren't some devil...

85
00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.180
who's trying to misuse the weapon.

86
00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:31.160
The Water 7 shipwrights haven't been passing down...

87
00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.580
for generations just how to build the weapon.

88
00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:39.200
Tom-san achieved
so many great things...

89
00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.340
and gave up everything to preserve
these blueprints for the future.

90
00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.510
At any rate, as long as there's a risk...

91
00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:47.440
that a woman named Nico Robin
can restore the weapon,

92
00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.320
the world needs
those blueprints to fight back.

93
00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.280
Hey, Spanda.

94
00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.400
What Tom-san and Iceburg
risked their lives to protect is...

95
00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:00.750
Hand them over to me already!

96
00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.690
the wish of this
weapon's architect—

97
00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.710
that is, if the ancient weapon fell
into the hands of an idiot like you...

98
00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.370
and started being used
to cause trouble,

99
00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:13.760
the architect would want another weapon
to be built in order to stop it.

100
00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:19.130
It's true that if you use Nico Robin,
you can revive the ancient weapon.

101
00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:21.130
Even if she doesn't
want to help you,

102
00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.780
as long as there's a chance
that she could be used,

103
00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.730
she's still dangerous.

104
00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.310
But she's got friends...

105
00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:32.260
who are willing to risk
their lives to protect her.

106
00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:33.490
So I'll...

107
00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.910
take a chance!

108
00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.900
I can think of only one way...

109
00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:43.870
to uphold the architect's wish in this situation.

110
00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.610
Just shut up and hand them
over to me already!

111
00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:48.090
Those are mine!

112
00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:07.850
You bastard!
What're you doing?!

113
00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.830
It's burned to a cinder!

114
00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.290
Dammit!

115
00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:15.820
I'm gonna kill you!

116
00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.780
Our five-year mission...

117
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.460
The blueprints were kept in order
to create a weapon to fight back...

118
00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:34.290
And you, the government,
came after them a second time.

119
00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.440
Essentially, something like
this should remain a secret,

120
00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.510
and so once it's revealed,
it has to be eliminated.

121
00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:46.120
Now, there's no longer a power to
fight back against the ancient weapon.

122
00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.950
If nothing is done and Nico Robin
falls into your hands,

123
00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:50.480
it'll be hopeless.

124
00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.110
But if the Straw Hats win...

125
00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.960
there won't be anything
left to you at all.

126
00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:01.910
I made a bet on their victory.

127
00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.410
How dare you mock me...?

128
00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:08.160
Seems like you want
to die here, too, huh?

129
00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.360
Bro!

130
00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.700
Bro!

131
00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.300
Big Bro Franky!

132
00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.260
Hey, look!

133
00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.680
Bro is at the Tower of Justice!

134
00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.550
Good! He's fine!

135
00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.260
That's Bro-waina!

136
00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.610
Bro!

137
00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:27.770
We came to rescue you-waina!

138
00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:31.190
We came with the Straw Hats!

139
00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.990
Sodom and Gomorrah
fought hard, too!

140
00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.190
Bro!

141
00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.070
Come home with us!

142
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.930
Are you hurt?!

143
00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.740
Y... You guys...

144
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.680
You idiots...

145
00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:47.240
Who asked you to come...

146
00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.280
to come rescue me?!

147
00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.040
You idiots!

148
00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.280
Bastards! I'm not crying!

149
00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.170
Shut up, you bastards!

150
00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.190
What are you, a demon?!

151
00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.770
Robin's waiting!

152
00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.650
Hurry up
and bring down the bridge!

153
00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.530
Oh, yeah, right.

154
00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.280
Hurry up, you bastards!

155
00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.380
That's right!

156
00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.240
Hurry up, you guys!
Or I'm gonna beat you up!

157
00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.320
Y-Yeah, you're right.

158
00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:29.870
I like when you're inconsistent
like that, too, Nami-san!

159
00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.870
Hey, Straw Hat!

160
00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.410
Looks like you looked out
for my underlings.

161
00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.300
But this time,

162
00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.310
I, their boss, the great Franky,

163
00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:43.300
will add my super fighting power
to you guys!

164
00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.050
Do what you want!

165
00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:49.270
I'm still holding what
you did to Usopp against you!

166
00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.560
Err... well,
he's right next to you...

167
00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.490
Cutty Flam...

168
00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.580
How dare you...

169
00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.320
burn my blueprints?!

170
00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:14.210
Ahh! Bro!

171
00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:19.170
Bro is falling into the falls!

172
00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.230
Franky!

173
00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:22.880
Hey, pirates!

174
00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.570
What?! Kokoro-san?!

175
00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.250
I heard everything!

176
00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.110
What're you guys wasting time for?!

177
00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.410
Wasting time?

178
00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.350
But the
bridge is only halfway down.

179
00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.600
Halfway is good enough!

180
00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.810
We'll be there in four seconds.

181
00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.710
What the hell is that?!

182
00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.640
Just dive in
toward the falls!

183
00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.160
That's... from earlier...!

184
00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.220
Is that the granny?

185
00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:49.260
What does she mean?

186
00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:50.330
I don't know.

187
00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.200
But she said
jump toward the falls.

188
00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.770
T-The sea train?!

189
00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.530
Why is it in the courthouse?!

190
00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:07.110
Chimney, go ahead and give that whistle a yank.

191
00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:08.430
Okay!

192
00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.520
That sounds like the sea train...

193
00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.440
What's the meaning of that smile?

194
00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:19.950
Chief Justice!

195
00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.940
Please get out of here!

196
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.150
Stop!

197
00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.670
Here we go!

198
00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.000
I knew it!

199
00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.880
Nooo!

200
00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:50.990
Rocketman can still run!

201
00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:54.460
Don't underestimate Tom's Workers,

202
00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.560
the legendary shipbuilders!

203
00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.940
R-Rocketman?!

204
00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.820
It's flying again!

205
00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.400
What?!

206
00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.590
They're coming!

207
00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.980
It's a waterfall!

208
00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.680
This brings back memories,
doesn't it, Tom-san?

209
00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.610
About helping that Roger guy...

210
00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:51.280
I'm DAMN proud that I did!

211
00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.370
I'm Luffy.

212
00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.220
I'm the man
who'll be the pirate king.

213
00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:54.850
Really?!

214
00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:55.370
Yeah.

215
00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.290
Roger...

216
00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.820
was an idiot like this kid,
too, wasn't he?

217
00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:07.060
And you helped him out.

218
00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:08.990
Seems like we didn't learn our lesson.

219
00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:14.200
Everyone in Tom's Workers
is helping this pirate kid.

220
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:20.730
You would've done the same,
wouldn't you, Tom-san?

221
00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.540
We're gonna hit the wall!

222
00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.070
W-We're gonna crash!

223
00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.800
Run!

224
00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:08.320
They're here...

225
00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.810
They're here!

226
00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:11.210
Dammit!

227
00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.680
Hey, come with me!

228
00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:18.240
If only I could get these
seastone handcuffs off...

229
00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:24.000
Now, I'm letting you loose, CP9!

230
00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:28.270
Beat the crap out of them
here, in the Tower of Justice!

231
00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.970
I'll give you permission
to destroy them!

232
00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.480
Lucci! Come with me!

233
00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:37.930
Protecting my life is your
top priority!

234
00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.280
Got that?!

235
00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:40.920
Funkfreed!

236
00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.880
All right, good boy.

237
00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.870
<b>Elephant Sword
Funkfreed
Elephant-Elephant Fruit</b>

238
00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:02.640
I've got this treasured sword,
in addition to CP9.

239
00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:06.470
When I calm down and think,
I've got nothing to be afraid of.

240
00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.960
Now, let's head to the Gates of Justice!

241
00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.840
Go ahead and get this woman
back if you can, Straw Hat!

242
00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.360
Big Bro Franky is okay!

243
00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:19.040
The Straw Hats have finally
reached the Tower of Justice!

244
00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.310
Bro is no longer a prisoner!

245
00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.120
Looks like he's gonna join in the fight!

246
00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.420
That's right!
He's that kind of person!

247
00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:27.980
Get them, Bro!

248
00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.730
Go! Straw Hat!

249
00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.490
We're leaving the rest
to you, Straw Hat.

250
00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.780
Hey, are you guys okay?!

251
00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.790
Kokoro, you old hag?!
Little ones?!

252
00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:42.660
What'd you come here for,

253
00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:46.440
bringing out a dangerous thing
like Rocketman?!

254
00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.830
W-Well, it saved me, too, but...

255
00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:51.000
Hey! Hey, Old Hag!
Hang in there!

256
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.700
Hey! I beg you! Don't die!

257
00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.790
Don't die!

258
00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:09.450
I've got a nosebleed.

259
00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:13.130
How could you walk away from this
sort of crash with just a nosebleed?!

260
00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:15.410
All right! We're here!

261
00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:17.860
Straw Hat...!

262
00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.130
Hello!

263
00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:21.570
Thanks, Monster Granny!

264
00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:24.310
Hey, you guys!
Get up already!

265
00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:25.990
That was nothing!

266
00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.400
You're rubber. Don't lump us in with you.

267
00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.900
Us flesh-and-blood humans were
forced to charge in like that.

268
00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.670
You think we're okay...?

269
00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:40.610
No way!

270
00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:42.140
Yup, they're all fine.

271
00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.850
You guys are all weirdos, too, so...

272
00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.640
Just sayin'.

273
00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.300
There are stairs over there!

274
00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.200
Let's hurry up and catch up to Robin!

275
00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.900
Wait.

276
00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:02.070
What the heck is that?!

277
00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.990
Chapapapa...

278
00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.400
We have been invaded.

279
00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.520
Even if you go
to the room you saw earlier,

280
00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.620
Nico Robin isn't there anymore,

281
00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.370
since Lucci took her to
the Gates of Justice.

282
00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:14.410
What?!

283
00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.900
Oh, and our chief is there, too.

284
00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.170
Oh, is that right?!

285
00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:22.820
Thanks for giving us
such valuable information.

286
00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:25.430
Chapapa... I spilled the beans...

287
00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:27.640
What a funny guy.

288
00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:28.800
Oh, well...

289
00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.920
They're headed there right now,

290
00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.910
but I won't tell you how to get there,

291
00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.780
and we, CP9,
won't let you go there, either.

292
00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:39.740
We have an order to annihilate you guys.

293
00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.610
Annihilation order...?

294
00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.820
Unless you defeat us,

295
00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.820
you won't be able
to set Nico Robin free.

296
00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:48.610
Yeah.

297
00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:51.290
You don't have to tell us that.
We're gonna do it anyway.

298
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.440
Chapapa...

299
00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.720
What a high-spirited guy.

300
00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.000
But let me tell you one more thing.

301
00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.020
What?! Do as you wish.

302
00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.870
Ah, thanks.

303
00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:03.720
Then, I'll speak frankly.

304
00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.970
Look at this!

305
00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.400
A key?

306
00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.430
What for?!

307
00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.690
This is the key to unlock...

308
00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.730
the seastone handcuffs on Nico Robin!

309
00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:16.080
Seastone?

310
00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:19.390
It's a stone that cancels out
devil fruit powers.

311
00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:22.450
I heard that it's as effective as when
ability users fall into the sea.

312
00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.080
So that's why Robin isn't fighting now,

313
00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.780
despite how strong she actually is.

314
00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.090
Yeah.

315
00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:30.730
Under normal circumstances,

316
00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:34.470
she isn't so weak that she'd helplessly
stay held captive by guys like that.

317
00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.420
She must be feeling frustrated.

318
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.960
I see.

319
00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:42.260
Even if you guys can rescue
Nico Robin by some chance,

320
00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.900
since seastone
is hard like diamonds,

321
00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:48.430
the handcuffs will be on her forever.

322
00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:50.500
Chapapa...

323
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.020
I spilled the beans again.

324
00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.350
He really is funny.

325
00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:58.590
If that's okay, keep trying to
rescue Nico Robin.

326
00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:01.030
Chapapapapa!

327
00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:02.990
Well, then...

328
00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.360
give that to us!

329
00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.910
Looks like he can use
that technique, too.

330
00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.960
Don't be so hasty.

331
00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:18.560
I didn't say that this is the right key.

332
00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.970
What?!

333
00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.550
It might be...

334
00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.460
for different handcuffs.

335
00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.700
Chapapa papa!

336
00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.810
There are five CP9 members,

337
00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:38.630
including me, in this tower.

338
00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.250
Each one has a key...

339
00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.250
One, two, come on!

340
00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.690
One, two, bad!

341
00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:46.240
and is waiting for you.

342
00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:46.240
Yow?!

343
00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:49.330
Then, until we defeat you all
and get the keys,

344
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.540
and try them on Robin's handcuffs,

345
00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.830
we won't know which one
is the right key?!

346
00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.510
How stupid... buying time?

347
00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:57.980
While we're fighting,

348
00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:01.350
you guys are trying to take Robin-chan
to the Gates of Justice, aren't you?!

349
00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:04.050
Quickly catching up with Robin
should be our priority.

350
00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:08.810
We'll first get Robin back,
and then worry about the key.

351
00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:11.230
Let's ignore that weirdo and hurry!

352
00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:12.060
Chapa!

353
00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:17.640
That weirdo

354
00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:13.900
Chapapa!

355
00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.280
You're smart.

356
00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.570
But if you do that,

357
00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:23.610
I'll ditch this key
into the sea! Chapapa!

358
00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:28.390
We're giving you a chance.

359
00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:28.950
See ya.

360
00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:31.530
Ah! Wait, you jerk!

361
00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:32.740
Hey, wait!

362
00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:35.890
You wait, dammit!

363
00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.340
Stop! Just a little bit longer!

364
00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:42.680
Just wait until we decide
what each of us will do!

365
00:22:43.100 --> 00:22:45.850
Ah! Let me go!

366
00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:48.250
Calm down, Straw Hat-kun.

367
00:22:48.250 --> 00:22:51.090
Let me go!

368
00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:51.090
Is Lucci that pigeon guy?

369
00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:53.160
Yeah, that's right.

370
00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:55.970
If he's with Robin-chan,

371
00:22:56.570 --> 00:22:59.230
we should let at least
Luffy go on ahead.

372
00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:00.420
Luffy.

373
00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:02.980
At any rate, you just
beat up the pigeon guy.

374
00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.500
Let me go! Let me go!

375
00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:08.380
There are six of us excluding Luffy.

376
00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:11.260
He said there are five CP9 members here.

377
00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:15.140
We'll get the five keys for Robin-chan's
handcuffs from them and go after Luffy.

378
00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:19.020
If Robin-kun goes through
the gates, it'll all be over.

379
00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:21.620
It's all a race against time!

380
00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:23.920
If we lose our fights,
it means we lose time!

381
00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:28.880
Everyone! Win at all cost!

382
00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:29.990
Yeah!

383
00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:32.840
Good luck!

384
00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:37.100
Pirate guys!

385
00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:43.800
Chimney? Gonbe?

386
00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:45.900
Where did they go?

387
00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:48.940
They were there up until just a bit ago!

388
00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:51.240
I'm sure I'll bump into them somewhere!

389
00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:54.620
I'm not gonna let you go to
the Gates of Justice!

390
00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.240
Robin!

391
00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:02.080
Help won't come, Nico Robin.

392
00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:09.120
They don't know how to get to the
Gates of Justice in the first place!

393
00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.810
Come out! You pigeon jerk!

394
00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:20.310
This is bad... before I fight...

395
00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:22.850
Where's the kitchen?!

396
00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.850
Coup de Boo!

397
00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:29.540
Because I used a bottle and
a half of cola for Coup de Boo,

398
00:24:29.540 --> 00:24:32.360
I've used more than two bottles today!

399
00:24:32.710 --> 00:24:36.280
Unless I fill up all three bottles,
I can't fight CP9!

400
00:24:38.080 --> 00:24:40.040
That area looks like a kitchen!

401
00:24:46.770 --> 00:24:50.360
Chapapapapa...

402
00:24:50.360 --> 00:24:52.210
I'm "Silent Fukuro"...

403
00:24:52.210 --> 00:24:54.130
I like rumors!

404
00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:56.100
Do you want the key?

405
00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:57.110
Dammit!

406
00:24:57.110 --> 00:24:58.850
I still haven't refilled my cola yet!

407
00:24:58.850 --> 00:25:00.360
Chapa...!

408
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:14.520
No one was in there.

409
00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:19.430
No one's here.

410
00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:23.160
Hmm, or here.

411
00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:26.870
All right, no one's here.

412
00:25:27.730 --> 00:25:31.260
What's going on?
I can't find anyone anywhere!

413
00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:33.400
If no one's around, that's fine, though.

414
00:25:38.790 --> 00:25:40.880
They must've gotten scared of me...

415
00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:42.970
Ahhh...!

416
00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:44.930
Someone's here!

417
00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:51.970
He's sleeping...

418
00:25:52.750 --> 00:25:54.700
Is he part of CP9, too?

419
00:25:56.330 --> 00:26:00.120
H-He's sleeping with the
key right in front of him!

420
00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:05.160
Couldn't this be a huge,
lucky chance?!

421
00:26:06.910 --> 00:26:10.840
I wonder what this
dungeon-like hallway is?

422
00:26:14.260 --> 00:26:16.470
Yoyoi!

423
00:26:16.980 --> 00:26:20.510
You damn pirate!

424
00:26:20.510 --> 00:26:26.230
You're doomed now that
I've caught you here!

425
00:26:26.620 --> 00:26:30.100
Wait...

426
00:26:30.100 --> 00:26:34.650
a second...!

427
00:26:36.690 --> 00:26:37.990
Yoyoi!

428
00:26:42.450 --> 00:26:44.080
How annoying...

429
00:26:44.080 --> 00:26:45.950
What about this room?!

430
00:26:48.760 --> 00:26:50.340
Dammit...

431
00:26:50.950 --> 00:26:53.000
No one's here, either.

432
00:27:01.630 --> 00:27:03.600
Please make yourself at home.

433
00:27:05.810 --> 00:27:09.270
Shall I... make some tea?

434
00:27:23.790 --> 00:27:25.870
Yes, please!

435
00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:38.340
You've already drawn your swords?

436
00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:43.300
They're just
crying out for blood.
